patrone-remote-desktop (0.3.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Work around Ubuntu bug 2171951, with a drop-in for GDM's headless session
    unit: it runs as a DynamicUser, which the system bus can't look up, so no
    headless session ever started. It now runs as the gdm account.
  * prepare-session gives up as soon as the desktop session's unit fails,
    instead of keeping the client on a black screen, and resets a unit that
    failed before.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:30:00 -0500

patrone-remote-desktop (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * NLA, as Windows does it: Remote Desktop Connection asks for the username
    and password itself, and the proxy checks NLA against a SAM file of NT
    hashes. A PAM hook (pam_exec, through pam-auth-update) keeps each
    remote-desktop member's hash current at every password sign-in and
    password change. The password NLA delivers is still checked with PAM at
    every connection. Remote Desktop Connection sends no password to a
    server without NLA, so 0.2's TLS-only sign-in never worked with it.
  * rdp-file no longer turns NLA off.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500

